en:
You know there's a bronze statue of the principal next to the main gate, right?
In the middle of the night, it starts moving all by itself.
The end.{p}

A heavy silence fell over the club room.
Was that really the end of Kazama's story{f:?|?}
{f:I|I} asked him, uneasy.
"...Um.
Is that really the end?"
"Yeah, that's right."{p}

A heavy silence fell over the club room.
Was that really the end of Kazama's story{f:?|?}
{f:I|I} asked him, uneasy.
"...Um.
Is that really the end?"
"Yeah, that's right.
{f:Got|If it's still not enough for you,} {f:some kind of complaint?|I could tell you more at my place, nice and slow...?}"
"No... {f:|n-}{f:it's not that I'm complaining.|no, thank you.}
{f:It's just that|If you'd just tell it} {f:it feels way too anticlimactic...|here and now...}"
{p}

"{f:I've told you two whole stories, and|Hm hm,} {f:you're still not satisfied?|are you feeling shy?}
...{f:Fine, then.|Aren't you adorable.}
{f:All right then,|Okay, you got it,} I guess I'll tell one more.
Truth is, this is one I didn't really want to tell..."
Kazama fell silent, as though brooding over something.
But he soon raised his head and began to talk.{p}

...Do you guys know someone in the third year named Teruo Koide?
Koide's possessed by a tanuki.
The end.{p}

"You're a demanding {f:one|little kitten}, aren't you?
Oh well, can't be helped. I never meant to tell four whole stories, though..."
Kazama clutched his head as if agonizing over it.
Would he finally tell me a really scary story this time{f:?|?}
After a long sigh, Kazama slowly began.
...Truth is, there's a girl in the third year named Tsukasa Sawami.{p}

A heavy silence fell over the club room.
Was that really the end of Kazama's story{f:?|?}
{f:I|I} asked him, uneasy.
"...Um.
Is that supposed to be a scary story?"
Up to now, however short, his stories had at least been scary{f:.|...}
{f:But|And yet,} what was {f:that one|that one}?{p}

"Um, please, I'm begging you.
This is a special feature on scary stories.
It's not about whether the school cafeteria food is awful or whatever.
I can't write an article with this.
For pity's sake{f:|}, think of it as helping {f:me|me} out and tell it seriously, won't you?"
Kazama {f:looked displeased|gave me a slimy, lingering look}.
{f:But|Ugh...} {f:there was no other way.|did I say that the wrong way?}
{f:I|What if he started in with} {f:kept at him.|"Oh, all right, for you, my lovey-dovey honey..."?}
{f:It seemed|Kazama} {f:he'd finally decided to talk.|silently lowered his eyes.}
{f:This time,|Huh?} {f:I hoped for a real scary story.|Is he actually going to tell it seriously...?}
...Oh, fine.
I've already told five whole stories, you know.{p}

"......{f:You're no fun,|Oh, come on,} {f:you know that.|you mustn't poke holes in it so fast.}
{f:Here I am going to all this trouble|I'm going to all this trouble} to build the mood{f:, and|, so} {f:why|come on,} {f:do you keep throwing cold water on it?|you've got to act a little scared.}
{f:Honestly,|...Oh, well,} {f:I swear...|you're just so cute...} {f:mutter mutter mutter|I'd forgive you anything}......"
Kazama was {f:muttering to himself|babbling nonsense}.
Why had Hino invited someone like this{f:?|?}
Maybe he was trying to make this whole project fail{f:|}{f:?|?}
{f:I|I} pulled myself together and decided to hear the third person's story.{p}

"Whoa!"
I jumped despite myself.
Then I looked where Kazama was pointing.{p}

...Nothing.
Of course there was nothing there.
Kazama had just been trying to scare us.{p}

A heavy silence fell over the club room.
Was that really the end of Kazama's story{f:?|?}
{f:I|I} asked him, uneasy.
"...Um.
Is that really the end?"{p}

"Yeah, that's right.
Well? Pretty scary, huh?"
"..........."
What on earth was with this guy{f:?|?}
Sure, if the story were true, you could say it was scary{f:, but|, but}...
A moving statue is just the kind of thing you hear in any silly rumor{f:.|.}
Was he making fun of {f:me|me}{f:?|...?}

"Go in through the student gate and head right and from around the seventh shrub you can see the back garden over the flowerbed and from there you walk about one hundred seventeen steps north toward the new school building and turn left and just short of the gym there stands solemnly the statue of the principal...
His eyebrows are raised sharply and he gazes on the students with loving eyes and deep within those eyes lies a passion for education and this finest of statues which ought to be the pride of us all..................moves on its own at night.
The end."{p}

But... {f:'lowly,' huh|I wonder if I've gained another fan}.
{f:Wahaha|Hm hm}!
{f:'A lowly one!'|Hm hm hm hm...}{p}{f:Kid|...Man}, {f:if you go around using corny words like that|club activities with you}{f:, girls will never go for you.| would sure be fun...}"{p}

"Hey, {f:don't glare at me with that scary face.|you're in Class 1-E, right?}
{f:I've|There, there}{f: carved precious time out of my last summer of high school| Next time}{f: to be here, you know.|, I'll come over to visit you.}
{f:A ladies' man like me|Or}{f: blew off a date with some babe to come here.| would you rather hang out somewhere outside school?}
...{f:Why don't you at least serve some tea|How about it}?"{p}

...
{f:I|I} sighed.
I didn't want to talk to this person anymore{f:.|.}
The principal's statue moves on its own at night.
That would do for the second of the seven wonders.
I surely wasn't going to get anything more out of him anyway{f:.|.}
There was nothing for it but to move on to the next story{f:.|.}
Trying not to look at Kazama, {f:I|I} said this:
"That concludes Kazama's story.
Now then, the next story..."{p}

Kazama stopped scratching his belly, lifted his rear off the seat, and leaned forward.
What was it?
What on earth {f:was|was} this guy?
He had a strange, intimidating air about him.
He was no ordinary person{f:.|.}
Maybe Hino had invited him for some deep reason{f:.|...}
This man gave off a dangerous scent...{p}

"{f:Hey|Mm}, {f:would you quit making such a show of being disgusted?|how awful.}
{f:I'm a third-year|Somebody farted, didn't they}{f:, the top of the school, you know.|? That's so annoying.}
{f:You mustn't forget your manners toward your seniors.|That's rude in front of a girl.}"
...
{f:Why on earth did Hino|Honestly, Kazama...}{f: invite someone like this?| when he's the one who farted...}
Kazama's attitude made up {f:my|my} mind.
{f:Manners, my foot.|Senior or not...}
I couldn't take any more of this{f:.|.}
Even if he really did know some amazing ghost story, I wanted nothing more to do with him.
{f:I|I} decided to hear the next person's story.
"Kazama, I'm terribly sorry.
Thank you for your wonderful story.
Please, take a nice long rest.
Oh, and you're welcome to go home, too.
Oh, I see, so you intend to stay here.
...Understood.
But if you get bored, feel free to go home anytime.
...Well then, let's move on to a different story. Next person, please..."{p}

Or so it felt.
{f:I|I} slowly looked around the room.
Everyone looked dissatisfied.
Huh?
Didn't the others have a bad feeling about it{f:?|?}
Did they want to hear the rest of Kazama's story{f:?|?}
...True, "The principal's statue moves at night. The end" might be a bit much.
But I couldn't very well say "On second thought, {f:tell me|tell me}" now.
Because...{p}

"Zzz... zzz..."
Kazama had fallen asleep at some point{f:.|.}
What on earth {f:is|is} this guy?
...Had he been sleepy all along{f:?|?}
Did he join the seven wonders interview, get sleepy, and just toss off some short, half-baked story{f:?|?}
{f:Still|But}... why did Hino invite someone like this?
...
Oh well.
There's no use thinking about it{f:.|.}
I {f:have to|have to} move on.
Under everyone's cold stares, {f:I|I} timidly spoke up.
"Um.
Shall we move on to the next story...?"{p}

{f:I|I} began to think about his life, love and death.......................................let's not.
I don't want to think about that.
Somehow, I'd lost all my motivation.
We're only on the second of the seven wonders, so why do I feel like this{f:?|?}
So sluggish.
I just don't feel like doing anything...
Is this the work of a spirit{f:?|?}
...
{f:No|No}, it's Kazama's fault{f:.|.}
Kazama's fault alone{f:.|.}
{f:Honestly|Geez}.
What on earth is this guy{f:?|?}
...Better not to get too involved with him{f:.|.}
Pulling myself together, {f:I|I} decided to hear the next story.
"Well then, let's go on to the next story.
The next person is..."{p}

Everyone must have sensed that this gathering was dangerous.
We never should have done an interview on the seven wonders.
And then, just as I was about to be the last to leave the deserted club room... something terrifying happened.{p}

"No. I said 'the end' properly a moment ago, didn't I?"
"Huh?★ But just now..."
"Oh, come on, all I said was {f:that I was disappointed in you|that I was hurt}."{p}

With that, Kazama took a photograph out of his pocket.
It was a photo of Kazama himself{f:.|.}
Does this guy always carry around photos of himself{f:?|...?}
"I'll give this to you.
It's a photo of the most beautiful, most noble being in this world.
Well? Aren't you happy?"
...That really made my head spin.{p}

Just how far was he going to take this clowning around?
Was he looking down on me just because I'm a first-year{f:?|?}
Enough. I'll leave someone like him alone and move on to the next story.
"Well then, the next story..."{p}

"You poor thing, you didn't realize that was the keyword."
Kazama gazed at {f:me|me} with pitying eyes.
But soon that turned into a {f:contemptuous|strange} look...{p}
